{"repositoryId":1380460766,"availability":"available","full":"ellokojavi/cairns","name":"cairns","description":"Cairns: installable, offline day-hike planner. Timed stops, turnaround cutoffs, forecast and GPS check-ins for Mailbox Peak, Mount Si, the Enchantments and other WA hikes.","category":"Other","language":"HTML","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-21T20:04:15Z","updated":"2026-10-15T05:10:33Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://ellokojavi.github.io/cairns/","topics":["gps","hiking","hiking-app","hiking-trails","offline","pwa","trail","washington","washington-state"],"demo":"https://ellokojavi.github.io/cairns/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T02:46:22.681Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T02:46:22.681Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T02:46:22.681Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-12T23:51:42.487Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-19T02:46:22.681Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["An installable, offline day-hike planner. Cairns are the piles of stones that mark the way.","Pick a route, set the date, start time and forecast, and Cairns times every stop, the turnaround cutoffs and the finish against sunset (or a parking gate that closes before dark). On the trail it checks you in from GPS and re-times the rest from your real pace. It works with no signal: the pages, maps and photos are stored on the phone, and GPS keeps working because position comes from satellites, not the network."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ellokojavi/cairns/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"d548ff404a646228750691ed39aca539d66bd22c1bc7216cb4783cff12e556b2","extractedAt":"2026-10-12T23:51:42.617Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T23:51:42.617Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"An installable, offline day-hike planner. Cairns are the piles of stones that mark the way.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ellokojavi/cairns/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requireme